# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Background {#background}"
msgstr "Pangunahing Kaalaman {#background}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This tutorial demonstrates how to implement **Approximate Quantum Compilation** using tensor networks (AQC-Tensor) with Qiskit to enhance quantum circuit performance. AQC-Tensor compresses deep Trotter circuits into shallower, more hardware-friendly circuits while preserving simulation accuracy.\n"
msgstr "Ipinapakita ng tutorial na ito kung paano ipatupad ang **Approximate Quantum Compilation** gamit ang mga tensor network (AQC-Tensor) kasama ang Qiskit upang mapabuti ang pagganap ng quantum circuit. Kino-compress ng AQC-Tensor ang mga malalim na Trotter circuit sa mas mababaw, mas hardware-friendly na mga circuit habang pinapanatili ang katumpakan ng simulation.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "How AQC-Tensor works {#how-aqc-tensor-works}"
msgstr "Paano Gumagana ang AQC-Tensor {#how-aqc-tensor-works}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Consider simulating a Hamiltonian $H$ for total time $t$ using $k$ Trotter steps. The full Trotter circuit is:\n"
msgstr "Isaalang-alang ang pagsimula ng isang Hamiltonian $H$ para sa kabuuang oras $t$ gamit ang $k$ na mga Trotter step. Ang buong Trotter circuit ay:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"U_{\\text{full}} = \\left[U_{\\text{Trotter}}(t/k)\\right]^k\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"U_{\\text{full}} = \\left[U_{\\text{Trotter}}(t/k)\\right]^k\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A naive approach uses few Trotter steps to keep circuit depth manageable, but this introduces significant Trotter error. AQC-Tensor resolves this tension by separating accuracy from depth:\n"
msgstr "Ang isang simpleng paraan ay gumagamit ng kaunting mga Trotter step upang mapamahalaan ang lalim ng circuit, ngunit nagdudulot ito ng malaking Trotter error. Nireresulba ng AQC-Tensor ang tensyong ito sa pamamagitan ng paghihiwalay ng katumpakan mula sa lalim:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Target circuit (high accuracy, deep):** Construct a Trotter circuit with many steps&mdash;say, $10k$&mdash;for the same evolution time. This circuit has far less Trotter error, but is too deep for hardware. Because it is only simulated classically as a matrix product state (MPS), depth is not a concern.\n"
msgstr "**Target circuit (mataas na katumpakan, malalim):** Bumuo ng isang Trotter circuit na may maraming hakbang&mdash;halimbawa, $10k$&mdash;para sa parehong oras ng ebolusyon. Ang circuit na ito ay may mas kaunting Trotter error, ngunit masyadong malalim para sa hardware. Dahil ito ay klasikal lamang na sinemulahin bilang isang matrix product state (MPS), ang lalim ay hindi isang alalahanin.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Ansatz circuit (low depth, parametrized):** Define a parametrized circuit $V(\\theta)$ with the same structure as a single-step Trotter circuit. Initialize it so that $V(\\theta_{\\text{init}}) = U_{\\text{Trotter}}(t/k)$, then iteratively optimize $\\theta$ so that $V(\\theta)$ reproduces the high-accuracy target state as closely as possible.\n"
msgstr "**Ansatz circuit (mababang lalim, parametrized):** Tukuyin ang isang parametrized circuit $V(\\theta)$ na may parehong istraktura tulad ng isang single-step Trotter circuit. I-initialize ito upang $V(\\theta_{\\text{init}}) = U_{\\text{Trotter}}(t/k)$, pagkatapos ay paulit-ulit na i-optimize ang $\\theta$ upang ang $V(\\theta)$ ay muling gawin ang high-accuracy target state nang malapitan hangga't maaari.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The result is a circuit that retains the depth of a single Trotter step but achieves the accuracy of many, making it feasible for near-term quantum hardware.\n"
msgstr "Ang resulta ay isang circuit na nagpapanatili ng lalim ng isang Trotter step ngunit nakakamit ang katumpakan ng marami, na ginagawa itong posible para sa malapit na hinaharap na quantum hardware.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "When to use AQC-Tensor {#when-to-use-aqc-tensor}"
msgstr "Kailan Gamitin ang AQC-Tensor {#when-to-use-aqc-tensor}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "AQC-Tensor is most effective when:\n"
msgstr "Ang AQC-Tensor ay pinaka-epektibo kapag:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Circuit depth exceeds hardware coherence times.** If a Trotter simulation requires more Trotter steps than the device can support, AQC-Tensor can compress the evolution into a shallower circuit.\n"
msgstr "**Ang lalim ng circuit ay lumagpas sa coherence time ng hardware.** Kung ang isang Trotter simulation ay nangangailangan ng mas maraming Trotter step kaysa sa kayang suportahan ng device, maaaring i-compress ng AQC-Tensor ang ebolusyon sa isang mas mababaw na circuit.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Entanglement remains classically tractable.** The total entanglement in a time-evolved state depends primarily on the evolution time $t$, not the number of Trotter steps $k$. This means a target circuit with $10k$ steps is typically no harder to represent as an MPS than one with $k$ steps, as long as $t$ is short enough for bond dimensions to stay manageable.\n"
msgstr "**Ang entanglement ay nananatiling klasikal na mapangangasiwaan.** Ang kabuuang entanglement sa isang time-evolved state ay pangunahing nakasalalay sa oras ng ebolusyon $t$, hindi sa bilang ng mga Trotter step $k$. Ibig sabihin nito, ang isang target circuit na may $10k$ na mga hakbang ay karaniwang hindi mas mahirap kumatawan bilang isang MPS kaysa sa isang may $k$ na mga hakbang, basta't ang $t$ ay sapat na maikli para mapamahalaan ang mga bond dimension.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**A natural ansatz exists.** Because the ansatz mirrors the structure of a Trotter circuit, it provides a physically motivated starting point with well-defined initial parameters, avoiding the convergence issues that can plague arbitrary variational ansatze.\n"
msgstr "**May natural na ansatz.** Dahil ang ansatz ay ginagaya ang istraktura ng isang Trotter circuit, nagbibigay ito ng isang physically motivated na simula na may malinaw na mga paunang parameter, na iniiwasan ang mga isyu sa convergence na maaaring manghirap sa mga arbitraryong variational ansatz.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This approach contrasts with generic circuit compression: rather than trying to approximate an arbitrary unitary with fewer gates, AQC-Tensor keeps the same gate structure and optimizes its parameters to reduce Trotter error. See the [AQC-Tensor documentation](https://qiskit.github.io/qiskit-addon-aqc-tensor/) for more information.\n"
msgstr "Ang pamamaraang ito ay kaibahan ng generic circuit compression: sa halip na subukang i-approximate ang isang arbitrary na unitary na may mas kaunting gates, pinapanatili ng AQC-Tensor ang parehong istraktura ng gate at ino-optimize ang mga parameter nito upang mabawasan ang Trotter error. Makita ang [dokumentasyon ng AQC-Tensor](https://qiskit.github.io/qiskit-addon-aqc-tensor/) para sa karagdagang impormasyon.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This tutorial guides you through the full state-preparation AQC-Tensor workflow: defining a Hamiltonian, generating Trotter circuits, compressing them via tensor-network optimization, and executing the result on IBM Quantum&reg; hardware.\n"
msgstr "Ginagabayan ka ng tutorial na ito sa buong state-preparation AQC-Tensor workflow: pagtukoy ng isang Hamiltonian, pagbuo ng mga Trotter circuit, pag-compress sa mga ito sa pamamagitan ng tensor-network optimization, at pagpapatupad ng resulta sa IBM Quantum&reg; hardware.\n"

